//@version=1
/* Dynamic requests: momentum rotation. The symbol requested on each bar
   is COMPUTED from data — whichever of SPY/QQQ has the stronger 20-bar
   momentum — so the request's child context changes row to row. A static
   request cannot express this: the pair is unknowable before the bar
   loop runs. Each distinct pair resolves once, on first encounter
   (run with TEA_LOG=debug to watch the two resolutions happen). */
indicator("Dynamic rotation")

// Two static requests: each candidate's momentum, computed with its own
// state inside its own child context.
spyMom = request.security("SPY", "D", ta.roc(close, 20))
qqqMom = request.security("QQQ", "D", ta.roc(close, 20))

// The leader is a SERIES string — known only per bar.
leader = spyMom > qqqMom ? "SPY" : "QQQ"

// The dynamic request: this bar's leader's smoothed price. The captured
// ta.ema keeps separate state per resolved pair (each child context owns
// its own frame tree).
price = request.security(leader, "D", ta.ema(close, 10))

// History on a dynamic result is parent-row-indexed: yesterday's ROW,
// whichever symbol served it — even across a rotation.
step = price - price[1]

plot(spyMom, title="SPY roc20")
plot(qqqMom, title="QQQ roc20")
plot(leader == "SPY" ? 1 : 2, title="leader (1=SPY 2=QQQ)")
plot(price, title="leader ema10")
plot(step, title="leader step")
